  "name": "REPETITIVE NERVE STIMULATION (RNS)",
  "code": "RNS",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<h3 data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1052\"><strong data-start=\"1031\" data-end=\"1050\">Interpretation:</strong></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1053\" data-end=\"1495\">\n<li data-start=\"1053\" data-end=\"1104\">\n<p data-start=\"1055\" data-end=\"1104\"><strong data-start=\"1055\" data-end=\"1069\">Normal RNS</strong>: No significant decrement noted.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1105\" data-end=\"1495\">\n<p data-start=\"1107\" data-end=\"1126\"><strong data-start=\"1107\" data-end=\"1123\">Abnormal RNS</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1129\" data-end=\"1495\">\n<li data-start=\"1129\" data-end=\"1234\">\n<blockquote data-start=\"1131\" data-end=\"1234\">\n<p data-start=\"1132\" data-end=\"1234\">10% decrement with low-frequency stimulation is suggestive of a <strong data-start=\"1196\" data-end=\"1231\">neuromuscular junction disorder</strong>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1237\" data-end=\"1388\">\n<p data-start=\"1239\" data-end=\"1388\">Presence of increment with high-frequency stimulation or post-exercise suggests <strong data-start=\"1319\" data-end=\"1385\">presynaptic disorder (e.g., Lambert-Eaton Myasthenic Syndrome)</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1391\" data-end=\"1495\">\n<p data-start=\"1393\" data-end=\"1495\">Decremental response without increment suggests <strong data-start=\"1441\" data-end=\"1492\">postsynaptic disorder (e.g., Myasthenia Gravis)</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
  "showInterpretation": true,
  "department": "672b3eace681c385cc85aac5",
  "isActive": true,
  "isOnboardedTest": false,
  "testCategory": [
    {
      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"482\"><strong data-start=\"454\" data-end=\"480\">Nerves/Muscles Tested:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"483\" data-end=\"616\">\n<li data-start=\"483\" data-end=\"535\">\n<p data-start=\"485\" data-end=\"535\">Right Ulnar nerve &ndash; Abductor digiti minimi (ADM)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"536\" data-end=\"573\">\n<p data-start=\"538\" data-end=\"573\">Right Accessory nerve &ndash; Trapezius</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"574\" data-end=\"616\">\n<p data-start=\"576\" data-end=\"616\">Other: _______________________________</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"618\" data-end=\"637\"><strong data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"635\">Findings:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"638\" data-end=\"1025\">\n<li data-start=\"638\" data-end=\"711\">\n<p data-start=\"640\" data-end=\"711\">At baseline, Compound Muscle Action Potentials (CMAPs) were recorded.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"712\" data-end=\"889\">\n<p data-start=\"714\" data-end=\"756\">With low-frequency stimulation (2&ndash;3 Hz):</p>\n<ul data-start=\"759\" data-end=\"889\">\n<li data-start=\"759\" data-end=\"851\">\n<p data-start=\"761\" data-end=\"851\"><strong data-start=\"761\" data-end=\"794\">Decremental response observed</strong>: ____ % (mention % drop from 1st to 4th/5th response).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"854\" data-end=\"889\">\n<p data-start=\"856\" data-end=\"889\">Significant if decrement &gt; 10%.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"890\" data-end=\"1025\">\n<p data-start=\"892\" data-end=\"955\">With high-frequency stimulation / post-exercise facilitation:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"1025\">\n<li data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"1025\">\n<p data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"1025\"><strong data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"993\">Incremental response observed</strong>: ____ % (mention if present).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1497\" data-end=\"1535\"><strong data-start=\"1501\" data-end=\"1533\">Conclusion :</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1536\" data-end=\"1753\">\n<li data-start=\"1536\" data-end=\"1665\">\n<p data-start=\"1538\" data-end=\"1665\">Findings are <strong data-start=\"1551\" data-end=\"1652\">consistent with a postsynaptic neuromuscular junction disorder (suggestive of Myasthenia Gravis).</strong><br data-start=\"1652\" data-end=\"1655\"><em data-start=\"1657\" data-end=\"1663\">(OR)</em></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1666\" data-end=\"1753\">\n<p data-start=\"1668\" data-end=\"1753\"><strong data-start=\"1668\" data-end=\"1751\">Normal study. No evidence of neuromuscular junction transmission defect on RNS.</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
